3	/**
4	 * DB-backed email rendering + the shared branded email shell.
5	 *
6	 * Templates live in the `EmailTemplate` table (admin-editable). Each row stores
7	 * a `subject` and an HTML *body* containing `{{variable}}` placeholders. At send
8	 * time we load the row, substitute the variables, and wrap the body in the
9	 * shared branded shell (header/footer). If a template is missing or disabled we
10	 * fall back to a minimal built-in default so a send never silently produces an
11	 * empty email.
12	 *
13	 * DESIGN (2026 refresh): a light, deliverability-safe theme. Real-world inbox
14	 * data shows light emails land in the primary tab more reliably than dark ones,
15	 * so the body is a soft violet-tinted background with a white content card and a
16	 * violet accent header carrying the Nxeon wordmark. Everything is table-based
17	 * with fully inline styles — Gmail/Outlook/Apple-Mail strip <style>, flexbox and
18	 * external CSS, so none of those are used. Gradients degrade to a solid
19	 * `background-color` fallback in clients that drop `background-image`.
20	 *
21	 * This module has NO dependency on `lib/mailer.ts` (mailer depends on it), which
22	 * keeps the import graph acyclic.
23	 */
